{"text": "inhabit", "etymologies": [{"etymologyHTML": "<p>From Old French <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"fro\">enhabiter</i>, from Latin <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">inhabitare</i> (<i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">in</i> + <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"la\">habitare</i>).\n</p>", "pos": [{"pos": "Verb", "definitions": [{"definition": "(transitive) To live or reside in.\n\n", "quote": [{"citation": "1813, Thomas Moore, The Last Rose of Summer:", "text": "O, who would inhabit this bleak world alone?"}], "relative": {}}, {"definition": "(transitive) To be present in.\n", "quote": [], "relative": {"Synonym": ["occupy"]}}]}]}], "pronunciation": [["IPA", "/\u026an\u02c8h\u00e6b\u026at/"]]}